  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": {
    "@es": "Preguntar por un sitio",
    "@en": "Ask for a site"
   },
   "texto": [
    {
     "@es": "Para parar a alguien: **Excuse me**. Luego: **Is there a bank near here?** (¿hay un banco por aquí cerca?) o **Where's the station?** (¿dónde está la estación?).",
     "@en": "To stop someone: **Excuse me**. Then: **Is there a bank near here?** (is there a bank around here?) or **Where's the station?** (where is the station?)."
    },
    {
     "@es": "**Near** = cerca. **Far** = lejos. **Is it far?** = ¿está lejos?",
     "@en": "**Near** = close. **Far** = far away. **Is it far?** = is it far away?"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": {
    "@es": "Dar indicaciones",
    "@en": "Provide indications"
   },
   "texto": [
    {
     "@es": "Las indicaciones se dan con el **imperativo**, que es el verbo tal cual, sin sujeto: **Go straight on** (siga recto), **Turn left** (gire a la izquierda), **Turn right** (gire a la derecha).",
     "@en": "The indications are given with the **imperativo**, which is the verb as, without subject: **Go straight on** (go straight), **Turn left** (turn left), **Turn right** (turn right)."
    },
    {
     "@es": "Para negar: **Don't turn left** (no gire a la izquierda).",
     "@en": "To deny: **Don't turn left** (do not turn left)."
    },
    {
     "@es": "Para situar: **on the left** (a la izquierda), **on the right** (a la derecha), **opposite** (enfrente de), **next to** (al lado de).",
     "@en": "To place: **on the left** (left), **on the right** (right), **opposite** (opposite), **next to** (next to)."
    }
   ]
  },
